# No commits on protected branches

NEVER run `git commit` or `git push` while HEAD is `master`, `develop`, or `main`.
NEVER push a refspec that updates those branches (`origin master`, `HEAD:master`, etc.).

This applies **even if the user explicitly asks** to commit or push on the current branch when that branch is protected.

Instead: create/switch to a feature branch, commit there, push that branch, open a PR.

A Cursor `beforeShellExecution` hook (`~/.cursor/hooks/block-master-develop-git.py`) denies these commands.
